      "dcterms:title": "Complexity, action, and black holes",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Browna, Adam R.",
        "Robertsb, Daniel A.",
        "Susskinda, Leonard"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20160512",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.04993",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Our earlier paper “Complexity Equals Action” conjectured that the quantum computational complexity of a holographic state is given by the classical action of a region in the bulk (the “Wheeler-DeWitt” patch). We provide calculations for the results quoted in that paper, explain how it ﬁts into a broader (tensor) network of ideas, and elaborate on the hypothesis that black holes are the fastest computers in nature. arXiv:1512.04993v2 [hep-th] 10 May 2016",
